[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4241842248","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118480#issuecomment-4241842248","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118480","id":4241842248,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc781WBI","user":{"login":"SharkyRawr","id":246984,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0Njk4NA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/246984?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SharkyRawr","html_url":"https://github.com/SharkyRawr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SharkyRawr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SharkyRawr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SharkyRawr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SharkyRawr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SharkyRawr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SharkyRawr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SharkyRawr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SharkyRawr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SharkyRawr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-14T06:56:34Z","updated_at":"2026-04-14T06:56:34Z","body":"I had the same or similar issue, try this:\n\nAccording to PR https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102987 \n- For editor: run/platforms/linuxbsd/prefer_wayland must be enabled.\n- For project: display/display_server/driver.linuxbsd set to \"wayland\" (X11 is still set chosen when \"default\" is selected).\n\nThat at least silenced the warning i got:\n\n```\n   WARNING: servers/display/display_server.cpp:1307 - HDR output is not supported by this display server.\n```\n\nHowever the docs talk about an HDR indicator showing up in the toolbar, next to view menu, which doesn't show up for me (https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/tutorials/rendering/hdr_output.html#hdr-output-in-the-godot-editor); so maybe all it did is silence the warning.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4241842248/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":1,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4244403920","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118480#issuecomment-4244403920","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118480","id":4244403920,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc78_HbQ","user":{"login":"fichtenmayermario","id":275420323,"node_id":"U_kgDOEGqUow","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/275420323?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fichtenmayermario","html_url":"https://github.com/fichtenmayermario","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fichtenmayermario/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fichtenmayermario/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fichtenmayermario/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fichtenmayermario/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fichtenmayermario/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fichtenmayermario/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fichtenmayermario/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fichtenmayermario/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fichtenmayermario/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-14T13:50:51Z","updated_at":"2026-04-14T13:50:51Z","body":"Okay,\nthe editor setting indeed switches the Display Server Support.\nI must have missed it in my Ubuntu 26.04 beta test, as the example works now!\nNo warnings, no errors, HDR works. Finally!\n\nBut with my \"old\" workhorse Ubuntu 25.04 I still get no window support for HDR.\nI intent to switch to the final version of Ubuntu 26.04 anyways, so my main problem is solved.\n\nMaybe I'm wrong, but are there minimum requirements on operating system level?\n\nAnd yes, I can't find that HDR indicator in the Linux version either.\n\nThank you for pointing out my oversight!\nNow I can finally use it!\nWell, in two weeks...","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4244403920/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4262962584","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118480#issuecomment-4262962584","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118480","id":4262962584,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7-F6WY","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-16T19:50:15Z","updated_at":"2026-04-16T19:50:15Z","body":"> But with my \"old\" workhorse Ubuntu 25.04 I still get no window support for HDR.\n> Maybe I'm wrong, but are there minimum requirements on operating system level?\n\nI'm actually not aware of any minimum system requirements besides Wayland operating in HDR mode. So if you've been able to successfully enable HDR mode on your screen in Wayland's display settings, Godot should also work with HDR mode and if it doesn't, that may be a bug, either with documentation or the behaviour in Godot.\n\n> And yes, I can't find that HDR indicator in the Linux version either.\n\nYou can find the HDR indicator in builds from `master`, but it hasn't been released in any of the dev builds yet. (4.7-dev5 will include this indicator).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4262962584/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4269584963","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118480#issuecomment-4269584963","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118480","id":4269584963,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7-fLJD","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-17T16:12:53Z","updated_at":"2026-04-17T16:12:53Z","body":"@fichtenmayermario Please let us know if you still aren't able to get HDR output working in Godot with Ubuntu 25.04 when HDR output is enabled in your OS display settings and is working well for other apps. As you know, make sure to follow [each step on the instructions](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/tutorials/rendering/hdr_output.html#enabling-hdr-output-in-your-project), especially item number 4: \"Configure the [Display Server Driver.linuxbsd](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/classes/class_projectsettings.html#class-projectsettings-property-display-display-server-driver-linuxbsd) advanced project setting to wayland and enable the [Prefer Wayland](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/classes/class_editorsettings.html#class-editorsettings-property-run-platforms-linuxbsd-prefer-wayland) editor setting.\"","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4269584963/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4270166794","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118480#issuecomment-4270166794","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118480","id":4270166794,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7-hZMK","user":{"login":"fichtenmayermario","id":275420323,"node_id":"U_kgDOEGqUow","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/275420323?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fichtenmayermario","html_url":"https://github.com/fichtenmayermario","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fichtenmayermario/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fichtenmayermario/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fichtenmayermario/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fichtenmayermario/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fichtenmayermario/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fichtenmayermario/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fichtenmayermario/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fichtenmayermario/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fichtenmayermario/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-17T17:55:42Z","updated_at":"2026-04-17T17:55:42Z","body":"Short answer because busy day schedule.\nSo far the problem remains.\nI packed the working example under U26.04, copied and unpacked it over to U25.04 - still not working.\nJust checked all settings again.\n\nMaybe it is a driver issue? (under 25.04 I use Nvidia's 570.195.03 driver)\nOr are you using a newer Vulkan extension which is absent in older drivers?\n\nI hope I can do a bit of more debugging myself on Sunday.\nSo far I have the impression that nobody else has this problem.\nSounds more like a me problem.\n\n<img width=\"2905\" height=\"1687\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/485708c1-49e1-4026-97cb-722e4fa4b64b\" />","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4270166794/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4270262150","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118480#issuecomment-4270262150","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118480","id":4270262150,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7-hweG","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-17T18:11:29Z","updated_at":"2026-04-17T18:11:29Z","body":"Thanks for sharing! No problem about the busy schedule. This is all very helpful.\n\n@ArchercatNEO Any thoughts on why Wayland HDR output might work on Ubuntu 26.04, but not work on Ubuntu 25.04?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4270262150/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4270345422","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118480#issuecomment-4270345422","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118480","id":4270345422,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7-iEzO","user":{"login":"ArchercatNEO","id":108980279,"node_id":"U_kgDOBn7oNw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/108980279?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO","html_url":"https://github.com/ArchercatNEO","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-17T18:23:36Z","updated_at":"2026-04-17T18:26:02Z","body":"During testing we found that GNOME had broken HDR which we couldn't resolve on our end because of https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/mutter/-/issues/4438. `target_luminance` is relevant for us since ~~those are the values we use for reference/max luminance~~ that's how we get max luminance.\n\nSome googling said Ubuntu 25.04 had GNOME 48 which I'm assuming didn't contain the bug fix, while Ubuntu 26.04 has a version of GNOME which does contain the bug fix (seeing as the issue has been closed).\n\nNo idea why blender HDR would work in GNOME 48 if the bug was indeed present but otherwise that's my preliminary theory.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4270345422/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4270388243","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118480#issuecomment-4270388243","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118480","id":4270388243,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7-iPQT","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-17T18:30:14Z","updated_at":"2026-04-17T18:30:14Z","body":"It's possible that Blender is fine without a maximum luminance. Unlike Godot, which depends on this for a number of Environment effects, Blender probably doesn't need to know what the maximum value is and simply renders a very large dynamic range, letting the screen simply clip or apply its own tonemapping.\n\nAlso sounds like there's probably no way around it, but since this is a bug in GNOME that already has a fix that's being rolled out... maybe this github issue is all the documentation we need to have surrounding this behaviour...","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4270388243/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4270394119","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118480#issuecomment-4270394119","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118480","id":4270394119,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7-iQsH","user":{"login":"ArchercatNEO","id":108980279,"node_id":"U_kgDOBn7oNw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/108980279?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO","html_url":"https://github.com/ArchercatNEO","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-17T18:31:14Z","updated_at":"2026-04-17T18:31:14Z","body":"To confirm if this is the case please run `wayland-info` (I don't know the Ubuntu package for this, it might be `wayland-utils`) and look for a `target_luminances` field. If the values you get are reasonable (i.e. the ones you have calibrated) then there is some other issue. If they are zero (as the linked issue suggests) this is just the GNOME bug and there's nothing we can do.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4270394119/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4270628492","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118480#issuecomment-4270628492","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118480","id":4270628492,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7-jJ6M","user":{"login":"fichtenmayermario","id":275420323,"node_id":"U_kgDOEGqUow","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/275420323?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fichtenmayermario","html_url":"https://github.com/fichtenmayermario","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fichtenmayermario/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fichtenmayermario/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fichtenmayermario/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fichtenmayermario/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fichtenmayermario/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fichtenmayermario/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fichtenmayermario/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fichtenmayermario/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fichtenmayermario/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-17T19:12:05Z","updated_at":"2026-04-17T19:12:05Z","body":"wayland-info doesn't show any luminance information at all (or I missed the correct parameter).\nBut knowing that at least a fixed Gnome 48 or later version is necessary is all I wanted to know.\nAs I'll switch to Ubuntu 26.04 / Gnome 50 anyways, this bug doesn't effect me anymore.\nFor others this information might be useful though.\n\nDo I have to close this issue, or does someone else?\nThis was my first bug report.\nThank you very much for your help!\n\n[wayland-info.txt](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/26838307/wayland-info.txt)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4270628492/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4270663872","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118480#issuecomment-4270663872","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118480","id":4270663872,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7-jSjA","user":{"login":"ArchercatNEO","id":108980279,"node_id":"U_kgDOBn7oNw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/108980279?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO","html_url":"https://github.com/ArchercatNEO","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-17T19:18:18Z","updated_at":"2026-04-17T19:18:18Z","body":"Annoyingly the version of `wayland-info` you have access to doesn’t include more recent updates that print additional information about wp-color-management. I don’t know of an equivalent which would print this information but I’m guessing this is very likely the problem.\n\nIn terms of documentation I don’t know if the fix was in GNOME 49 or GNOME 50 so we should probably test those before adding a minimum requirement. As far as I know all other compositors which support HDR also implemented it correctly in the first release so GNOME should be the only one we need to document (though if we wanted to document the minimum versions for other compositors I would not be against it)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4270663872/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4270813999","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118480#issuecomment-4270813999","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118480","id":4270813999,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7-j3Mv","user":{"login":"fichtenmayermario","id":275420323,"node_id":"U_kgDOEGqUow","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/275420323?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fichtenmayermario","html_url":"https://github.com/fichtenmayermario","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fichtenmayermario/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fichtenmayermario/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fichtenmayermario/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fichtenmayermario/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fichtenmayermario/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fichtenmayermario/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fichtenmayermario/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fichtenmayermario/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fichtenmayermario/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public",